"answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off on June 15th and an initial budget of $500,000. The project has secured a strategic partnership with TechInnovate for AI research. The team is currently gathering innovative ideas, particularly from R&D, to enhance data visualization tools using AI, with proposals due by July 20th. A significant milestone was reached with the successful completion of the testing phase for a secure file sharing prototype, ahead of schedule. The executive board has approved a total budget of $2 million to cover research, development, and marketing. The next phase involves user interface enhancements starting in October, followed by a celebration on October 10th. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November. Additionally, security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, will be updated effective January next year."
